# .vercelignore
#
# Vercel's Python functions package the whole repo unless files/directories are
# excluded. With this repository teaching every phase of FraudGuard (notebooks,
# 144 MB raw data, EDA artifacts, presentation figures, Docker/Compose configs,
# the local Python tooling in .venv, .agents, .freebuff and the deployed React
# frontend), the unstripped upload easily exceeds the Vercel function-size limit.
#
# This file focuses the deployment on the **FastAPI backend**. It replaces the
# greedy all-in upload with the small set of files the API actually needs to start
# and serve `/predict`/health/alerts.
#
# The trained model is intentionally **not** excluded; without it the API starts
# degraded and `/predict` returns 503.
#
# `.gitignore` already keeps most of this *out of Git*. Vercel packages both
# tracked and untracked files by default, so the same shape has to be expressed
# here explicitly.

# --- Python runtime tooling (huge, never executed on the function platform) ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Version control / agent / platform config ---
.git/
.gitignore
.agents/
.freebuff/
.neon/
.vscode/
.idea/
skills-lock.json

# --- Frontend (deployed separately on Vercel; not part of the Python backend) ---
frontend/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/dist/

# --- Data and notebooks (Phase 2 EDA / training inputs; not runtime inputs) ---
data/
notebooks/
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Raw and processed data specifically ---
data/raw/
data/processed/

# --- Logs ---
*.log
logs/

# --- Training / EDA / evaluation / benchmarking assets used to *build* the model,
# --- not to serve it. One trained artifact is what production needs. ---
artifacts/eda/
artifacts/performance/
artifacts/model_results/
artifacts/.gitkeep

# --- One-off scripts: build the model or run experiments, not the deployed API ---
scripts/

# --- Repository-local Docker / Compose / CI config ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.sqlite.yml

# --- Frontend tooling at repo root that is not the Python backend ---
package-lock.json
package.json
neon.ts

# --- Testing / load tooling ---
tests/
